From 22b27a78dfe1bc18930b7185b4c6299225b162ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XRoar dev <dev@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:06:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 46/49] cart: emulate CoCo Max and X-Pad input devices

Add selectable CoCo Max Hi-Res Input Module and X-Pad GT-116 cartridge profiles. Both source input from the right virtual joystick, including its two buttons.

CoCo Max retains the hardware A/D pipeline: every read returns the preceding conversion and starts the selected conversion. The normal CoCo address is $FF90-$FF97; on a CoCo 3 it uses the documented hardware modification at $FF60-$FF67 so it cannot collide with GIME registers.

X-Pad is already a low-address device at $FF60-$FF62 and therefore works on a CoCo 3 without a hardware modification. Its X read atomically latches the matching Y and status values, and its status follows the GT-116 bit definitions.
